ress tensor; this leads to a questionable relation of symmetry of forces. We show how a reinterpretation of the concept of partial stress tensor avoids this problem. The usual balance equations hold, but the distinction between the new stress tensor and the old leads to a different interpretation of boundary data.</p>", "DOI": "10.1090/qam/99715", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2016, 12, 14]], "date-time": "2016-12-14T19:26:33Z", "timestamp": 1481743593000}, "page": "527-530", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 16, "title": ["On balance of forces for mixtures"], "prefix": "10.1090", "volume": "30", "author": [{"given": "Morton E.", "family": "Gurtin", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Marion L.", "family": "Oliver", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "William O.", "family": "Williams", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "14", "reference": [{"key": "1", "unstructured": "R. M. Bowen, Continuum theories of mixtures, Report No. 45, RDTE No. 1B062113A660, BRL, Aberdeen Proving Grounds, Md., June 1971."}], "container-title": ["Quarterly of Applied Mathematics"], "original-title": [], "language": "en", "link": [{"URL": "http://www.ams.org/qam/1973-30-04/S0033-569X-1973-99715-7/S0033-569X-1973-99715-7.pdf", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}, {"URL": "https://www.ams.org/qam/1973-30-04/S0033-569X-1973-99715-7/S0033-569X-1973-99715-7.pdf", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 4, 20]], "date-time": "2026-04-20T14:15:15Z", "timestamp": 1776694515000}, "score": 1, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ams.org/qam/1973-30-04/S0033-569X-1973